course: dictionary
lesson: 14332
title: Obtainable: able to be got
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Obtainable means you are able to get it or buy it. When a notice says «The tickets are obtainable from the office», it tells you that you can get tickets there. The words around it give the clue: the office is where you go to get something.
explain: Obtainable can also mean possible to reach. In «The highest obtainable score on the quiz was 10», the words highest and score tell you that 10 is the most points anyone could get. Ask yourself: could I get this? If yes, obtainable is a good fit.
explain: Formal writing often uses obtainable instead of available or can be got. «Books are easily obtainable from the library» means the library has them and they are simple to borrow. Easily obtainable means very simple to get.
fact: Obtainable means able to be got or bought.
fact: «The tickets are obtainable from the office.» Here it means you can get the tickets at the office.
fact: «The highest obtainable score» means the most points you could possibly get.
fact: Useful phrases: easily obtainable, obtainable from, the maximum obtainable.
fact: Obtainable is often used in formal notices and exam language, where it means much the same as available.
exercise: «The tickets are obtainable from the office.» Where can you get the tickets? | At the seaside | Under your bed | *At the office | In the sky
exercise: «The highest obtainable score on the quiz was 10.» What does obtainable mean here? | *The most points you could get | The lowest points you could get | A kind of quiz game | The number of questions in the quiz
exercise: Which word could replace obtainable in «The tickets are obtainable from the office»? | *available | broken | sleepy | heavy
test: «Books are easily obtainable from the library.» What does easily obtainable mean? | Only for teachers | Impossible to find | *Very simple to get | Written in pencil
test: Which phrase means the most points you could possibly get? | the broken clock | a quiet voice | *the maximum obtainable | the lowest mark
exam: Which sentence uses obtainable correctly? | The sky is obtainable in the dark. | My shoes are obtainable when I sleep. | The stone was obtainable under the sea. | *Tickets are obtainable from the office before five o'clock.
